      "worked_solution": "The measure of $∠DAE$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠BAE)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠BAD).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nm∠DAE={120}^{∘}-{80}^{∘}={40}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLet's add this to our diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133186/assets/df3e0be0d89947829ede0fbd55b19cb8d0a13c77cf5ece6c25933254d7cce29f.png)\n\nWe can now find the measure of $∠CAE:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CAE & =m∠CAD+m∠DAE \\\\  & ={60}^{∘}+{40}^{∘} \\\\  & ={100}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
